# Alio's fine-tuned medical model, for Ollama.
#
# Build it with:
#
#   ollama create alio-medical -f backend/Modelfile.alio-medical
#
# That registers it locally under the short name `alio-medical`, which is what
# OLLAMA_MODEL defaults to in medical_ai.py — so nothing else needs configuring.
# The first build downloads ~3.4 GB from HuggingFace and takes a few minutes.
#
# Then switch the backend over by adding this to backend/.env:
#
#   USE_LOCAL_OLLAMA=1
#
# See backend/README.md → "Running on the fine-tuned model" for the whole
# procedure, including how to confirm it is actually being used.
#
# FROM names the published artifact rather than a file path. An earlier version
# of this file pointed at a .ollama blob inside one teammate's Windows home
# directory, which meant it only worked on that one machine. If you ever need a
# local GGUF instead, point FROM at the file — but do not commit that.

FROM hf.co/aarony630/alio-medical:Q4_K_M

PARAMETER temperature 0.4
PARAMETER top_p 0.9
PARAMETER stop "<turn|>"
PARAMETER num_ctx 2048

SYSTEM "You are a medical assistant that explains health information in plain language for family members. Always reply in JSON when the prompt requests structured output."
